Subject: [PATCH] Preserve unmanaged fallback and account for failed
 original-client attempts

Repair the complete four-case runtime batch from final39211469726 (203of207 passed). Record failed fake commands against the matching original backend before availability failure while preserving wrong-socket rejection. An existing-only legacy probe with no client may return the original Unavailable plain shell; available daemons still require a positive UUID match and pinned-context absence still fails. Correct only the newly added locator field of the original unmanaged fixture to None; retain every prior fixture value, call and assertion. Extend the existing legacy-match regression with absent-client fallback, no attachment and no invented locator checks. No compiler recipe, policy or test-selector changes.
